---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/asbj02.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Basic Earnings Per Share (基本的1株当たり当期純利益)" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Profit Attributable to Owners of Parent (親会社株主に帰属する当期純利益)" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Weighted Average Shares — the Treasury Share Exclusion" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Diluted Earnings Per Share (潜在株式調整後1株当たり当期純利益)" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Basic EPS" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Diluted EPS With Stock Acquisition Rights" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A single, comparable per-share profitability metric</div>
        <div class="principle">EARNINGS PER SHARE (1株当たり当期純利益, EPS) distills a company's overall profitability down to a SINGLE, PER-SHARE figure, allowing INVESTORS to compare profitability across companies of DIFFERENT sizes and across TIME, independent of share count changes. ASBJ Statement No. 2 sets out how to calculate BOTH a "BASIC" EPS figure and, where potentially dilutive securities exist, a "DILUTED" EPS figure reflecting the FULL potential dilution of existing shareholders' claims.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Companies with publicly traded (or otherwise widely held) shares</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to companies REQUIRED (or electing) to disclose EPS figures — typically listed companies, though the calculation methodology is relevant WHEREVER EPS disclosure is presented.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Basic Earnings Per Share (基本的1株当たり当期純利益)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Profit attributable to owners of parent, divided by weighted average shares</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">BASIC EPS is calculated as PROFIT ATTRIBUTABLE TO OWNERS OF PARENT (Section 4) for the period, DIVIDED by the WEIGHTED AVERAGE number of shares of Common Stock OUTSTANDING during the period (Section 5) — the foundational, undiluted per-share profitability measure.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Profit Attributable to Owners of Parent (親会社株主に帰属する当期純利益)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Consolidated profit, excluding the portion belonging to non-controlling interests</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">For CONSOLIDATED financial statements, the numerator used is PROFIT ATTRIBUTABLE TO OWNERS OF PARENT — CONSOLIDATED net profit for the period, AFTER excluding the portion attributable to NON-CONTROLLING INTERESTS (非支配株主持分) — ensuring EPS reflects only the earnings genuinely available to the PARENT company's own shareholders.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Weighted Average Shares — the Treasury Share Exclusion</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Treasury shares held during the period are excluded from the denominator</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">The WEIGHTED AVERAGE share count EXCLUDES any TREASURY SHARES (自己株式, see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 1 poster) held by the company DURING the period — since treasury shares do NOT represent an outstanding claim of an EXTERNAL shareholder, they are NOT counted in the EPS denominator for the period they are held.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Diluted Earnings Per Share (潜在株式調整後1株当たり当期純利益)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Reflecting the maximum potential dilution from convertible or option-like instruments</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Where a company has issued instruments with the POTENTIAL to convert into, or be exercised for, additional Common Stock — STOCK ACQUISITION RIGHTS (新株予約権, broadly equivalent to stock options/warrants), convertible bonds, or similar — DILUTED EPS incorporates the ADDITIONAL shares that WOULD result if those instruments were CONVERTED/EXERCISED, adjusting BOTH the numerator (for any related profit effect, e.g. interest expense saved on converted bonds) and the denominator (for the additional potential shares) — PROVIDED the effect is genuinely DILUTIVE (reduces EPS).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Basic EPS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Excluding treasury shares from the denominator</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A company with treasury shares held throughout the year</div><div class="wk-body">A company reports profit attributable to owners of parent of ¥900,000,000 for the year. It has 10,000,000 shares of Common Stock issued, of which 500,000 are held as treasury shares throughout the entire year.</div><div class="wk-answer">Weighted average shares OUTSTANDING = 10,000,000 − 500,000 = <strong>9,500,000 shares</strong>. Basic EPS = ¥900,000,000 ÷ 9,500,000 = <strong>¥94.7 per share</strong> (approximately) — the treasury shares are EXCLUDED from the denominator for the entire period they were held.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Diluted EPS With Stock Acquisition Rights</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Incorporating potential additional shares</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Outstanding stock acquisition rights</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example (Basic EPS ¥94.7, 9,500,000 weighted average shares), the company has outstanding stock acquisition rights that, if exercised, would result in 300,000 ADDITIONAL shares being issued, with no offsetting profit adjustment required.</div><div class="wk-answer">Diluted weighted average shares = 9,500,000 + 300,000 = <strong>9,800,000 shares</strong>. Diluted EPS = ¥900,000,000 ÷ 9,800,000 = <strong>¥91.8 per share</strong> (approximately) — LOWER than basic EPS, reflecting the DILUTIVE effect of the potential additional shares from the stock acquisition rights.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 2 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Basic and diluted EPS, presented on the face of the Statement of Income</span><span>The basis of calculation, including the numerator and weighted average share count used</span><span>Nature of potentially dilutive securities and why they were (or were not) included in the diluted calculation</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a potentially dilutive instrument is genuinely dilutive (reduces EPS) and should be included in the diluted calculation</span></div></div>
        <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Weighted average calculation for shares issued or reacquired partway through the period</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 33</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 2)</span><span>IFRS (IAS 33)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Basic EPS formula</span><span>Profit attributable to owners of parent ÷ weighted average shares</span><span>Same formula — converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Treasury share exclusion</span><span>Excluded from the denominator</span><span>Excluded from the denominator — converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Diluted EPS mechanics</span><span>Adjusts for potentially dilutive instruments, if-converted/treasury-stock-style methods</span><span>Same general approach — converged</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">EPS is one of the MOST genuinely converged areas between J-GAAP and IFRS, reflecting ASBJ's long-standing convergence project with the IASB — the core mechanics travel almost directly between the two frameworks.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every EPS event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Basic/Diluted EPS disclosure</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Presented on the face of the Statement of Income</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 1</span><span>Supplies the treasury share concept excluded from the EPS weighted average denominator</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 22</span><span>Consolidated Financial Statements — supplies the non-controlling interests concept used to determine profit attributable to owners of parent</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Profit attributable to owners of parent (親会社株主に帰属する当期純利益)</div><div class="glossary-def">Consolidated profit for the period, excluding the portion attributable to non-controlling interests.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Stock acquisition rights (新株予約権)</div><div class="glossary-def">Rights entitling the holder to acquire shares of the company, a common source of potential dilution for diluted EPS purposes.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Weighted average shares outstanding</div><div class="glossary-def">The time-weighted average number of shares outstanding during a period, excluding treasury shares held.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
